## Per-work-unit verdicts

w1 "Audit Result Detail metadata and receipt fields":
   Confirmed. The audit is the body of this w0 log; verdicts for
   w2-w5 follow.

w2 "Collapse empty or nearly empty environment summaries":
   Already-fixed. `ResultDetail.tsx:184-194` builds `environmentRows`
   by filtering each environment field to a `null` / present pair;
   lines 273-281 already render either the present rows or a single
   "Environment metadata was not recorded for this run." placeholder.
   The "multiple adjacent cards repeating missing values" anti-pattern
   the TODO targets is not present in the current code. Mark this
   work unit deferred (no diff needed); document the verdict here so
   future audits do not re-raise the same observation.

w3 "Group missing receipt fields behind disclosure":
   Confirmed, with SCOPE DEVIATION. The receipt rendering lives in
   `components/RunReceipt.tsx`, which the original TODO `scope_limit`
   does not list. `ResultDetail.tsx:336` simply mounts
   `<RunReceipt detail={detail} ... />`; the section / row layout that
   needs grouping behind a disclosure is entirely inside RunReceipt.
   Per the per-TODO workflow's "Diverged" rule, the YAML's
   `scope_limit.only_modify` is widened in the same PR to include
   `results-explorer/src/components/RunReceipt.tsx` and its existing
   test `results-explorer/src/components/__tests__/RunReceipt.test.tsx`.
   The `must_preserve` invariants ("Receipt/provenance remains
   available for audit") are honored — recorded fields stay in the
   default view; only the missing rows move behind the disclosure.

w4 "Apply shared display labels to Result Detail enums":
   Confirmed. Two surfaces render raw enum strings today:
   - `ResultDetail.tsx:459-461` defines a local `formatDisplayToken`
     that is functionally `formatEnumLabel` from `lib/displayLabels.ts`.
     It is applied to `trust_label` and `validation_status` for the
     summary "Trust / validation" metric card. Replace the local
     helper with the shared `formatTrustLabel` /
     `formatValidationStatus` so curated labels render
     ("maintainer run", "not applicable") instead of the underscore /
     dash form.
   - `RunReceipt.tsx` renders `detail.trust_label`,
     `detail.visibility`, `detail.validation_status`, and
     `detail.cost_status` as raw strings (lines 64-66, 87). Replace
     with the shared formatters from `lib/displayLabels.ts`.

w5 "Cover complete and sparse Result Detail metadata cases":
   Confirmed. Tests need to:
   - assert RunReceipt renders "maintainer run" / "public (curated)"
     after the formatter swap (existing test fixture has
     "maintainer-run" / "public-curated");
   - add a sparse-metadata case that verifies missing receipt rows
     are NOT visible in the default view but are reachable via the
     disclosure;
   - keep the existing complete-metadata case (every section
     renders).

